{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:0b79bdac44c5f646","name":"Sith Wyrm","source":{"id":"source:reference-0b79bdac44c5f646","title":"Sith Wyrm","revision":20537,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:02:35Z","sha256":"c44e9908704f85bcf89194b800c2946228ae46c65eedbb6a85656a6f12245587","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20537","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Sith%20Wyrm&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-0b79bdac44c5f646","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Sith Wyrm is the result of Naga Sadow's experimentation on a larval ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exogorth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exogorth?action=edit&redlink=1"}," that has attached itself to the hull of his battleship en route to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin 4"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin_4","referenceId":"reference:5f008a1b1f754b64"},". He mutated the creature, and it eventually became worshiped as a living god by the primitive ",{"tag":"a","children":["Massassi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Massassi","referenceId":"reference:5369acf6589c1958"}," people who guarded the temples on the moon's surface.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Sith Wyrm is an enormous creature capable of devouring smaller creatures whole. It relies on base instincts and simply eats anything that gets in its way. Like the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exogorth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exogorth?action=edit&redlink=1"}," on which it was derived, a Sith Wyrm can survive for thousands of years on a modest diet. The huge tunnels that it creates by burrowing through the ground can undermine structures and riddle a planet with meandering passageways, some of which might open up to secret warrens and forgotten underground structures.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Sith Wyrm Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Only one Sith Wyrm has been encountered to date, but it's possible that other Sith Lords have created similar monstrosities. The Sith Wyrm can serve as a template for other enormous creatures designed to serve as living war machines, terrorizing entire ecosystems with their ravenous hunger.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Sith Wyrm Statistics (CL 15)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal Subterranean ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 16\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +8; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +12\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 26 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 26), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 40, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 25\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 296, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 15, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 95\n"